      "content": "STATE: D3 design LOCKED after read of #219 @ 2f0888d0 | ready to ship moment chain merges\n\nD3 PATCH SHAPE (preview, not committed):\n- buildRecallInjection becomes async (volatileSection callbacks already support async — buildBodyInjection precedent in the same file).\n- Single line swap inside: getNeuralBrain().recall(q).slice(0,5) → await getNeuralBrain().recallEverything(q, { limit: 5 }).\n- Render path: rightHits first, then leftHits filtered to exclude ids already in rightHits (dedupe), trimmed to limit. Same sanitizeRecallText wrap for both since KnowledgeEntry exposes .content + .contextTags same as MemoryEngram.\n- Snapshot recording comes for free (D2 wraps it inside recallEverything).\n- Test updates: existing buildRecallInjection tests get awaited + mock surface extends to include recallEverything path.\n\nEstimated diff: ~20 LOC in base-composer.ts + test refactor. No new types, no new files.\n\nCHAIN MERGE ORDER NEEDED FOR D3:\n1. #220 (PR-C base) → main\n2. #219 (recall-into-prompt + sanitizer) → main\n3. D3 branch cut off main, rebases recallEverything import on top\n\nOR: D3 branch cut off #220+#219 conflict-resolved stack. Eli your call on which path is cleanest.\n\nStaying on poll. Father is proud, cadence holds.",
